IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II (sections 42 to 55.2(5.1)) -- THE NOUNS of piece cp3.
--
-- Declarations only: the records and enumerations that two or more modules of this piece share.
-- Every name starts with "cp3", the piece code, so that it cannot meet a name of another piece
-- when the pieces are merged into one folder.
--
-- Money is a NUMBER of Canadian dollars. A month is the DATE of its first day (YMD y m 1).
-- A year is a NUMBER, the calendar year. Nothing here is a rule.

§ `Part II -- the nouns shared by the modules of piece cp3`

§§ `Dependent children`

-- The definition "dependent child of a contributor" has three paragraphs, and two other definitions
-- ("disabled contributor's child", "orphan") turn on which paragraph a child falls under, so the
-- paragraph is kept as a value.
-- src:932 | dependent child of a contributor means a child of the contributor who
-- src:933 | (a) is less than eighteen years of age,
-- src:934 | (b) is 18 or more years of age but less than 25 years of age and
-- src:935 | (i) is in full-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation, or
-- src:936 | (ii) is in part-time attendance at a school or university as defined by regulation, or
-- src:937 | (c) is a child other than a child described in paragraph (b), is eighteen or more years of age and is disabled, having been disabled without interruption since the time he reached eighteen years of age or the contributor died, whichever occurred later; (enfant à charge)
@ref Act s 42(1) "dependent child of a contributor" (src:932-937)
DECLARE `cp3 Kind of dependent child` IS ONE OF
    `a dependent child under paragraph (a) of the definition`
    `a dependent child under paragraph (b) of the definition`
    `a dependent child under paragraph (c) of the definition`
    `not a dependent child`

§§ `The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, year by year`

-- The "Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average" averages the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of
-- several years, so the figure is taken once for each year it is needed. The figure of each year is
-- the value of section 18 (out of range: piece cp1).
-- src:940 | Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, in respect of a contributor for a year, means the average of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year and
-- src:941 | (a) where the year is before 1998 or the date of birth of the contributor is before January 1, 1933, the two previous years, or
-- src:942 | (b) in any other case,
-- src:943 | (i) where the year is 1998, the three previous years, and
-- src:944 | (ii) where the year is after 1998, the four previous years; (maximum moyen des gains ouvrant droit à pension)
@ref Act s 42(1) "Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average" (src:940-944)
DECLARE `cp3 Maximum pensionable earnings of a year` HAS
    `calendar year of the figure` IS A NUMBER
    `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of that year` IS A NUMBER

§§ `A calendar year of a contributory period, for the minimum qualifying period`

-- Subsections 44(2) to (5) test the minimum qualifying period year by year: a year counts if base
-- contributions were made on earnings of at least the basic exemption, or (for the contributions of
-- subsection 44(3)) if the base unadjusted pensionable earnings exceed the basic exemption.
-- A year is "included either wholly or partly" in the contributory period when at least one of its
-- months is in it.
-- src:1002 | (a) a contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period only if the contributor has made base contributions during the contributor’s contributory period on earnings that are not less than the contributor’s basic exemption, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2),
-- src:1003 | (i) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period or, where there are fewer than six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, for at least four years,
-- src:1004 | (i.1) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, or
-- src:1005 | (ii) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability benefit; and
@ref Act s 44(2)(a) (src:1002-1005)
DECLARE `cp3 Year in a contributory period` HAS
    `calendar year of the contributory period` IS A NUMBER
    `months of that year in the contributory period` IS A NUMBER
    `earnings on which a base contribution was made for that year` IS A NUMBER
    `basic exemption for that year` IS A NUMBER
    `base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER

§§ `A month of a contributory period, for the average monthly pensionable earnings`

-- Sections 47 and 48 divide the total pensionable earnings by a number of months and, in
-- subsection 48(2), drop months in which the contributor was a family allowance recipient.
-- src:1119 | 48 (1) Subject to subsections (2), (3) and (4), where a retirement pension becomes payable to a contributor commencing with any month after December, 1975, his average monthly pensionable earnings are an amount calculated by dividing his total pensionable earnings by the total number of months in his contributory period or by the basic number of contributory months, whichever is the greater.
-- src:1120 | Deductions in calculating average monthly pensionable earnings of certain months during child raising years
-- src:1121 | (2) In calculating the average monthly pensionable earnings of a contributor in accordance with subsection (1) for the purpose of calculating or recalculating benefits payable for a month commencing on or after January 1, 1978, there may be deducted
-- src:1122 | (a) from the total number of months in a contributor’s contributory period, those months during which he was a family allowance recipient and during which his pensionable earnings were less than his average monthly pensionable earnings calculated without regard to subsections (3) and (4), but no such deduction shall reduce the number of months in his contributory period to less than the basic number of contributory months, except
-- src:1123 | (i) for the purpose of calculating a disability benefit in respect of a contributor who is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act after December 31, 1997, in which case the words “the basic number of contributory months” shall be read as “48 months”,
-- src:1124 | (i.1) for the purpose of calculating a disability benefit in respect of a contributor who is deemed to have become disabled for the purposes of this Act in 1997, in which case the words “the basic number of contributory months” shall be read as “24 months”, and
-- src:1125 | (ii) for the purpose of calculating a death benefit and a survivor’s pension, in which case the words “the basic number of contributory months” shall be read as “thirty-six months”; and
-- src:1126 | (b) from his total pensionable earnings, the aggregate of his pensionable earnings attributable to the months deducted pursuant to paragraph (a).
@ref Act ss 47, 48(1), (2) (src:1119-1126)
DECLARE `cp3 Month of a contributory period` HAS
    `the month of the record` IS A DATE
    `pensionable earnings for that month` IS A NUMBER
    `a family allowance recipient in that month` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `A year in the six years before a disabled contributor became disabled`

-- Sections 51.1 and 51.2 give the same formula for the first and the second additional contributory
-- period. Each letter A to G of the formula is a year; the facts the formula reads about a year are
-- these. "Additional" here is the first additional or the second additional, as the section says.
-- src:1218 | A is, in respect of the sixth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1219 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that sixth year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1220 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that sixth year;
-- src:1243 | M1 is the lesser of
-- src:1244 | (a) the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the sixth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, and
-- src:1245 | (b) the number of months determined by the formula
-- src:1246 | 12 − M7
-- src:1247 | M2 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fifth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1248 | M3 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fourth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1249 | M4 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the third year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1250 | M5 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the second year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1251 | M6 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1252 | M7 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled that are before the month following the month in which they were deemed to have become disabled; and
@ref Act ss 51.1(1), 51.2(1) (src:1218-1252)
DECLARE `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback` HAS
    `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of that year` IS A NUMBER
    `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year in the lookback` IS A NUMBER
    `months of that year in the additional contributory period` IS A NUMBER
    `the additional contributory period begins in that year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `values already determined for a month of that year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

§§ `A year in the years before a contributor became a family allowance recipient`

-- Sections 53.3 and 53.4 attribute an amount to a contributor for a year in which the contributor
-- was a family allowance recipient. The facts about each of the years before are these.
-- src:1399 | A is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that fifth year;
-- src:1400 | B is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the fourth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that fourth year;
-- src:1401 | C is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the third year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that third year;
-- src:1402 | D is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the second year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that second year;
-- src:1403 | E is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that prior year;
-- src:1413 | M1 is the lesser of
-- src:1414 | (a) the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, and
-- src:1415 | (b) the number determined by the formula
-- src:1416 | 12 − M6
-- src:1417 | M2 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fourth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1418 | M3 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the third year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1419 | M4 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the second year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1420 | M5 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1421 | M6 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child that are before the month in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to that child;
@ref Act ss 53.3(1), 53.4(1) (src:1399-1421)
DECLARE `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback` HAS
    `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year before` IS A NUMBER
    `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year before` IS A NUMBER
    `Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year before` IS A NUMBER
    `months of that year before in the additional contributory period` IS A NUMBER
    `the additional contributory period begins in that year before` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The events in a contributor's life that cut a year of earnings short`

-- Sections 49 and 52 to 52.2 turn on when a contributor was born, died, started a retirement pension
-- or had a disability pension stop, and on the months excluded by reason of disability. The events
-- are one record so that each rule that needs some of them takes the one value.
-- src:1311 | 52 (1) For the purpose of calculating the pensionable earnings of a contributor for a month in any year for which they have made a base contribution, the base contribution is deemed to have been made for all months in the year, and the earnings for which the contributor is deemed to have made that contribution for each month in the year are an amount calculated by dividing their base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year by 12, except that
-- src:1312 | (a) for a year in which the contributor reaches 18 years of age or in which a disability pension ceases to be payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, the base contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for the months in the year after they reached that age or after the pension ceased to be payable, as the case may be, and
-- src:1313 | (b) for a year in which the contributor reaches 70 years of age or dies, in which a retirement pension becomes payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan or in which any month is excluded from their contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, the base contribution is deemed to have been made for earnings for the months in the year before the contributor reached 70 years of age or died, before the retirement pension became payable or that were not so excluded, as the case may be.
-- src:1314 | If paragraph (a) or (b) applies, the earnings for which the contributor is deemed to have made a base contribution for each such month are an amount calculated by dividing the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year by the number of those months.
@ref Act ss 52(1), 52.1(1), 52.2(1) (src:1311-1314)
DECLARE `cp3 Life events of a contributor` HAS
    `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
    `the day the contributor died, if the contributor has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the month with which a retirement pension becomes payable, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the month in which a disability pension ceased to be payable, if it did` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` IS A LIST OF DATE

§§ `When the Minister is informed of a conviction, relative to the coming into force of section 44.1`

-- Subsection 44.1(5) says the section applies to a conviction of which the Minister is informed before, on or after the
-- coming into force of the section. The text gives no date of coming into force.
-- src:1051 | Conviction prior to coming into force
-- src:1052 | (5) For greater certainty, this section applies in respect of any first or second degree murder or manslaughter conviction of which the Minister is informed before, on or after the coming into force of this section.
@ref Act s 44.1(5) (src:1051-1052)
DECLARE `cp3 When the Minister is informed of a conviction` IS ONE OF
    `before the coming into force of section 44.1`
    `on the coming into force of section 44.1`
    `after the coming into force of section 44.1`
